course: dictionary
lesson: 10166
title: Tibetan: a word with three jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can change its job depending on the words around it. In «Yaks live on the Tibetan plateau, often above 4000 metres», Tibetan describes the plateau, so it is an adjective, a describing word. The word after it, plateau, tells you what it describes.
explain: Tibetan can also be a noun, a name for a person. «Many Tibetans abroad describe it as self-governing» means many people from Tibet. Tibetan can name a language too: the Tibetan language, written in its own script. Look at the words around it to find out which job it has.
explain: Read history sentences carefully, because people can disagree. «Tibet came under the control of the People's Republic in 1950–1951.» The Chinese government says Tibet has been part of China for centuries, while the Dalai Lama and many Tibetans describe it as historically independent. A careful reader notes both views and checks where each comes from.
fact: Tibetan means from or to do with Tibet, a high region in the Himalayas.
fact: A Tibetan is a person from Tibet, and the plural is Tibetans.
fact: Tibet is called «the roof of the world» because it is a very high plateau.
fact: Great rivers like the Yangtze and the Brahmaputra start in Tibet.
fact: Most Tibetans are Buddhists, and the Dalai Lama is their best-known religious leader.
exercise: In «Yaks live on the Tibetan plateau», what kind of word is Tibetan? | A verb, an action word | *An adjective, a describing word | The name of a person | A noun, the name of a thing
exercise: In «Many Tibetans abroad describe it as self-governing», what is a Tibetan? | A grey cloud | *A person from Tibet | A yak | A river in the Himalayas
exercise: What does «the Tibetan language» mean? | A type of rain | *The language of Tibet, written in its own script | A dog breed only | A kind of mountain
test: Why is Tibet called «the roof of the world»? | Because it has the most roofs in the world | *Because it is a very high plateau | Because it lies under the sea | Because it is flat and close to the sea
test: Which word means a person from Tibet? | Yangtze | *Tibetan | Tibetan plateau | Himalayas
exam: Two sentences describe Tibet's history differently: China says Tibet has been part of China for centuries, while the Dalai Lama describes it as historically independent. What should a careful reader do? | Pick the first view because it is longer | Skip the history and never think about it again | Decide one view is silly without reading more | *Note both views and check where each one comes from
